:Class SOAC ⍝ Simple OAuth Client

    ⍝ OAuth Client Configuration
    :field clientId           ⍝ OAuth client identifier
    :field clientSecret       ⍝ OAuth client secret (optional for PKCE)
    :field usePKCE            ⍝ Boolean: Enable Proof Key for Code Exchange
    :field flow               ⍝ OAuth flow type: 'authorizationCode' 'deviceCode' 'clientCredentials'

    ⍝ OAuth Provider Endpoints
    :field authUrl            ⍝ Authorization endpoint URL
    :field deviceUrl          ⍝ Device authorization endpoint URL
    :field tokenUrl           ⍝ Token exchange endpoint URL

    ⍝ Session State (set during flow execution)
    :field codeVerifier       ⍝ PKCE code verifier (only set if usePKCE=1)
    :field state              ⍝ CSRF protection state (set upon AuthorizeURL generation)

    ⍝ Constants
    :field private DFLT_POLL_INTERVAL←5      ⍝ Default polling interval (seconds)
    :field private DFLT_MAX_ATTEMPTS←300     ⍝ Default max polling attempts
    :field private SLOW_DOWN_INCREMENT←5     ⍝ Increase interval on slow_down (seconds)
    :field private CALLBACK_TIMEOUT←300      ⍝ Callback await timeout (seconds)

    ⍝ Logging Configuration
    :field enableLogging←0    ⍝ Enable debug logging

    ∇ r←GetState
      ⍝ Retrieve the current CSRF protection state value
      ⍝ Returns: State string (UUID) used for authorization request
      :Access public
      r←state
    ∇

    ∇ Log msg
      ⍝ Internal logging helper for debugging
      ⍝ Arguments:
      ⍝   msg - Message string to log
      ⍝ Output: Prints '[SOAC] msg' to console if enableLogging=1
      :Access private
      :If enableLogging
          ⎕←'[SOAC] ',msg
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ⍝ External Dependencies
    :field HttpCommand        ⍝ Reference to HttpCommand utility for HTTP operations
    :field Jarvis             ⍝ Reference to Jarvis web server framework
    :field public j           ⍝ Jarvis instance for callback server
    :field public trg         ⍝ Thread range for callback target for OAuth responses
    ⎕RL←(⍬ 2)                 ⍝ Initialize random number generator (Use OS Random Generator)

    ∇ r←New args
      ⍝ Create a new SOAC OAuth client instance
      ⍝
      ⍝ Arguments:
      ⍝   args - Configuration namespace with OAuth provider settings
      ⍝          Required: client.id, auth.authUrl or auth.tokenUrl
      ⍝          Optional: client.secret, client.flow, client.usePKCE, auth.deviceUrl
      ⍝
      ⍝ Returns:
      ⍝   New SOAC instance configured for specified OAuth flow
      :Access public shared
      :If 0∊⍴args
          r←##.⎕NEW⊃⊃⎕CLASS ⎕THIS
      :Else
          r←##.⎕NEW(⊃⊃⎕CLASS ⎕THIS)args
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ make1 args;vars;upgradeResp;_
      ⍝ Constructor: Initialize OAuth client with configuration
      ⍝ Validates flow type, sets up PKCE if enabled, loads dependencies
      :Access public
      :Implements constructor

      :If 0=#.⎕NC 'HttpCommand'
        #.HttpCommand←#.{⎕SE.SALT.Load 'HttpCommand'}⍬
        HttpCommand←#.HttpCommand
        upgradeResp←HttpCommand.Upgrade
        :If 1=⊃upgradeResp
          Log 'Upgraded HttpCommand: ',2⊃upgradeResp
        :ElseIf 0=⊃upgradeResp
          Log 'HttpCommand is on latest version: ',⍕HttpCommand.Version
        :Else
          Log 'Unable to upgrade HttpCommand: ',2⊃upgradeResp
        :EndIf
      :Else
        HttpCommand←#.HttpCommand
      :EndIf

      :If 0=#.⎕NC 'Jarvis'
        _←HttpCommand.Fix 'github/Dyalog/Jarvis/Source/Jarvis.dyalog' #
      :EndIf

      ⍝ Extract configuration from flat namespace
      flow←args ⎕VGET ⊂'flow' 'authorizationCode'
      :If ~(⊂flow)∊'authorizationCode' 'deviceCode' 'clientCredentials'
        ⎕SIGNAL ⊂('EN' 11) ('Message' 'Invalid flow specified')
        →0
      :EndIf

      :If flow≡'authorizationCode'
        usePKCE←args ⎕VGET ⊂'usePKCE' 1
      :Else
        usePKCE←args ⎕VGET ⊂'usePKCE' 0
      :EndIf
      :If ~(∨/0 1∘∊)usePKCE
        ⎕SIGNAL ⊂('EN' 11) ('Message' 'usePKCE must be boolean')
      :EndIf

      clientId←args ⎕VGET 'clientId'
      clientSecret←args ⎕VGET ⊂'clientSecret' ''
      authUrl←args ⎕VGET ⊂'authUrl' ''
      tokenUrl←args ⎕VGET ⊂'tokenUrl' ''
      deviceUrl←args ⎕VGET ⊂'deviceUrl' ''

      Jarvis←##.Jarvis
      HttpCommand←##.HttpCommand
      j←Jarvis.New''
    ∇

    ∇ destruct;_
      :Implements destructor
      :Trap 0
          _←j.Stop
      :EndTrap
    ∇

    ∇ r←GetAuthorizationURL args;params;url
      ⍝ Generate OAuth authorization URL with PKCE support
      ⍝
      ⍝ Arguments:
      ⍝   args.redirectUri - Callback URL for OAuth redirect
      ⍝   args.scope - Space-separated string or array of scope values
      ⍝   args.state - (optional) CSRF protection state; auto-generated if not provided
      ⍝   args.custom - (optional) Additional custom parameters
      ⍝
      ⍝ Returns:
      ⍝   Namespace with authorization URL and state:
      ⍝   {url: 'https://...' state: 'generated-uuid'}
      :Access public
      ValidateFlow 'authorizationCode'
      params←(
          client_id:clientId
          response_type:'code'
          redirect_uri:args.redirectUri
          scope:args.scope
          state: ⎕VGET⊂'args.state' genState
      )

      ⍝ Validate state before assignment
      :If params.state≡''
          ⎕SIGNAL ⊂('EN' 5) ('Message' 'state is empty')
      :EndIf

      state←params.state

      ⍝ Add PKCE (Proof Key for Code Exchange) parameters if enabled
      ⍝ PKCE prevents authorization code interception attacks
      :If usePKCE
        codeVerifier←genCodeVerifier              ⍝ Generate random 43-128 char string
        params.code_challenge←genCodeChallenge codeVerifier  ⍝ SHA256 + base64url encode
        params.code_challenge_method←'S256'       ⍝ Indicate SHA256 hash method
      :EndIf

      params.scope←NormalizeScope params.scope

      params ⎕NS ⎕VGET⊂'custom'()
      url←authUrl,'?',HttpCommand.UrlEncode params

      ⍝ Return namespace with URL and state
      r←(url: url ⋄ state: state)
    ∇

    ∇ r←StartDeviceFlow args
      ⍝ Start OAuth device authorization flow
      ⍝
      ⍝ Arguments:
      ⍝   args.scope - Space-separated string or array of scope values
      ⍝
      ⍝ Returns:
      ⍝   Namespace with device flow parameters:
      ⍝   On success: {success:1 device_code:'..' user_code:'..' verification_uri:'..' interval:N}
      ⍝   On error: {success:0 error_description:'...' error:'...'}
      :Access public
      ValidateFlow 'deviceCode'
      params←(
          client_id: clientId
          client_secret: clientSecret
          response_type: 'device_code'
          scope: args.scope
      )


      ⍝ Device flow doesn't use state parameter (no browser redirect to validate)
      ⍝ Set to 'null' to maintain consistent internal state tracking
      state←⊂'null'

      ⍝ PKCE is not standard for device flow but can be enabled if provider supports it
      :If usePKCE
        ⎕←'WARNING: UsePKCE is NOT standard in device flow'
        codeVerifier←genCodeVerifier
        params.code_challenge←genCodeChallenge codeVerifier
        params.code_challenge_method←'S256'
      :EndIf

      params.scope←NormalizeScope params.scope

      httpArgs←(
        URL: deviceUrl
        TranslateData: 1
        Method: 'POST'
        Params: params
        ContentType: 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded'
      )

      h←HttpCommand.Do httpArgs
      r←ProcessHttpResponse h
    ∇

    ∇ r←WaitForToken args;interval;deviceCode;maxAttempts;attempt
      ⍝ Wait for token completion in device authorization flow
      ⍝
      ⍝ Arguments:
      ⍝   args.deviceCode - Device code from InitiateDeviceFlow
      ⍝   args.interval - (optional) Polling interval in seconds (default: 5)
      ⍝   args.maxAttempts - (optional) Maximum polling attempts (default: 300)
      ⍝
      ⍝ Returns:
      ⍝   Namespace with token or error:
      ⍝   On success: {success:1 access_token:'..' token_type:'..' ...}
      ⍝   On error: {success:0 error:'...' error_description:'...'}
      ⍝   Automatically handles 'authorization_pending' and 'slow_down' responses
      :Access public
      ValidateFlow 'deviceCode'

      ⍝ Extract parameters from args
      deviceCode←args ⎕VGET 'deviceCode'
      interval←args ⎕VGET ⊂'interval' DFLT_POLL_INTERVAL
      maxAttempts←args ⎕VGET ⊂'maxAttempts' DFLT_MAX_ATTEMPTS

      attempt←0
      r←()

      :While attempt≤maxAttempts
        attempt+←1

        ⍝ Wait before polling (except first attempt)
        :If attempt>1
          ⎕DL interval
        :EndIf

        ⍝ Attempt to get token
        r←GetToken (deviceCode:deviceCode)

        ⍝ Check if we got a token successfully
        :If r.success
          →0  ⍝ Success - return with token
        :EndIf

        ⍝ Handle error cases
        :If 0≠r.⎕NC'error'
          :Select r.error
          :Case 'authorization_pending'
            ⍝ User hasn't authorized yet, continue polling
          :Case 'slow_down'
            ⍝ Increase polling interval on slow_down response
            interval+←SLOW_DOWN_INCREMENT
          :Case 'expired_token'
            ⍝ Device code has expired
            r.error_description←'Device code expired'
            →0
          :Case 'access_denied'
            ⍝ User denied authorization
            r.error_description←'User denied authorization'
            →0
          :Else
            ⍝ Unknown error, stop polling
            →0
          :EndSelect
        :Else
          ⍝ If there's an error_description but no error field, stop
          →0
        :EndIf
      :EndWhile

      ⍝ Max attempts reached
      :If ~r.success
        r.success←0
        r.error←'timeout'
        r.error_description←'Maximum polling attempts reached'
      :EndIf
    ∇


    ∇ r←ParseUrl url
      ⍝ Parse URL query string into namespace
      ⍝
      ⍝ Arguments:
      ⍝   url - URL string with query parameters
      ⍝
      ⍝ Returns:
      ⍝   Namespace with query parameters as fields
      ⍝   Example: 'http://example.com?code=abc&state=xyz' → {code:'abc' state:'xyz'}
      :Access public
      ⍝ Processing steps: (1) Drop everything before '?', (2) URL decode,
      ⍝ (3) Split on '&', (4) Split each on '=', (5) Set as namespace fields
      (r←⎕NS'')⎕VSET↓2↑[2]↑'='(≠⊆⊢)¨'&'(≠⊆⊢)HttpCommand.UrlDecode(('?'(⊃∘⍸⍷)⊢)↓⊢)url
    ∇

    ∇ r←ProcessHttpResponse h
      ⍝ Standardized HTTP response handler
      ⍝ Returns namespace with success flag and response data
      :Access private
      r←()
      :If 2≠⌊0.01×h.HttpStatus
          r.success←0
          r.error_description←'HTTP Error: ',⍕h.HttpStatus
          :If 0≠≢h.Data
            r←r ⎕NS h.Data
          :EndIf
          →0
      :EndIf
      :If 0≠h.Data.⎕NC'error_description'
          r.success←0
          r←r ⎕NS h.Data
      :Else
          r.success←1
          r←r ⎕NS h.Data
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ r←NormalizeScope scope
      ⍝ Convert scope array to space-separated string
      ⍝ If scope is string, return as-is; if array, join with spaces
      :Access private
      :If (⊂≢⊆)scope
          r←1↓∊' ',¨scope
      :Else
          r←scope
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ ValidateFlow required;msg
      ⍝ Validates current flow matches required flow
      ⍝ Signals error if mismatch
      :Access private
      :If flow≢required
          msg←'This method is only available in ''',required,''' flow'
          ⎕SIGNAL ⊂('EN' 11) ('Message' msg)
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ r←GetToken args;code;deviceCode;redirectUri;params;h
      ⍝ Exchange authorization code or device code for access token
      ⍝
      ⍝ Arguments:
      ⍝   For authorization code flow: (code: 'auth_code' ⋄ redirectUri: 'callback_url')
      ⍝   For device code flow: (deviceCode: 'device_code')
      ⍝
      ⍝ Returns:
      ⍝   Namespace with token or error:
      ⍝   On success: {success:1 access_token:'..' token_type:'..' expires_in:N ...}
      ⍝   On error: {success:0 error:'...' error_description:'...'}
      :Access public

      :Section Parse Arguments
      ⍝ Validate args is a namespace
      :If 9≠⊃⎕NC 'args'
        ⎕SIGNAL ⊂('EN' 11) ('Message' 'GetToken requires namespace argument')
      :EndIf

      ⍝ Extract parameters based on flow
      :Select flow
      :Case 'authorizationCode'
        code←args ⎕VGET 'code'
        redirectUri←args ⎕VGET 'redirectUri'
        :If redirectUri≡''
          ⎕SIGNAL ⊂('EN' 5) ('Message' 'redirectUri is required for authorization code flow')
        :EndIf

      :Case 'deviceCode'
        deviceCode←args ⎕VGET 'deviceCode'
        code←deviceCode  ⍝ Use deviceCode as code for backward compatibility in params

      :Case 'clientCredentials'
        ⎕SIGNAL ⊂('EN' 11) ('Message' 'clientCredentials flow not yet implemented')

      :Else
        ⎕SIGNAL ⊂('EN' 11) ('Message' 'No flow specified')
      :EndSelect

      :Section Build HTTP Request
      ⍝ Build HTTP request parameters
      params←(
          URL: tokenUrl
          Params:(
              grant_type:''
              client_secret: clientSecret
              client_id:clientId
          )
          Method:'POST'
          ContentType:'application/x-www-form-urlencoded'
          TranslateData:1
          Debug:0
      )

      :If params.Params.client_secret≡''
        params.Params.⎕EX 'client_secret'
      :EndIf

      :Section Configure Flow-Specific Parameters
      :Select flow
      :Case 'authorizationCode'
        params.Params.code←code
        params.Params.grant_type←'authorization_code'
        params.Params.redirect_uri←redirectUri

      :Case 'deviceCode'
        params.Params.device_code←code
        params.Params.grant_type←'urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:device_code'
      :EndSelect

      :If usePKCE
        params.Params.code_verifier←codeVerifier
      :EndIf

      :Section Execute Request
      h←HttpCommand.Do params
      r←ProcessHttpResponse h
    ∇

    ∇ cbUrl←StartCallbackServer port;cl;jr
      ⍝ Start local HTTP server to receive OAuth callback
      ⍝
      ⍝ Arguments:
      ⍝   port - Port number for callback server (e.g., 3000)
      ⍝
      ⍝ Returns:
      ⍝   Callback URL string to use as redirectUri in authorization request
      ⍝   Format: 'http://localhost:PORT/auth'
      ⍝   Server runs until AwaitCallback completes or destructor is called
      :Access public
      ValidateFlow 'authorizationCode'
      j.AllowGETs←1
      j.Port←port
      j.Paradigm←'REST'
      (cl←⎕NS'').Get←AuthorizeCallback
      cl.Post←AuthorizeCallback
      j.CodeLocation←cl
      trg←⎕TALLOC 1 'oauthcallback'
      j.Logging←0
      j.Debug←1
      jr←j.Start
      :If 0≠⊃jr
          cbUrl←''
          ⎕SIGNAL ⊂('EN' 100) ('Message' ('Jarvis failed to init: ',2⊃jr))
      :EndIf
      cbUrl←'http://localhost:',(⍕port),'/auth'
    ∇

    ∇ r←WaitForCallback;dltid;_
      ⍝ Wait for OAuth callback from authorization server
      ⍝
      ⍝ Returns:
      ⍝   Namespace with callback result:
      ⍝   On success: {success:1 code:'..' state:'..'}
      ⍝   On error: {success:0 error_description:'...'}
      ⍝   Automatically validates state parameter for CSRF protection
      ⍝   Timeout: 5 minutes
      ⍝   Stops callback server and cleans up thread after completion
      :Access public
      ValidateFlow 'authorizationCode'
      ⍝ Launch timeout thread that will signal error if timeout elapses
      ⍝ Thread runs in background and puts timeout error to thread pool if triggered
      dltid←{
          _←⎕DL CALLBACK_TIMEOUT
          _←(success:0 ⋄ error_description:'timeout reached')⎕TPUT trg+0.1
      }&⍬
      ⍝ Block waiting for callback result (from AuthorizeCallback or timeout thread)
      r←⎕TGET trg+0.1
      ⍝ Kill timeout thread if callback succeeded or failed for other reason
      :If r.success
          ⎕TKILL dltid  ⍝ Success - kill timeout thread
      :ElseIf ~'timeout reached'≡r.error_description
          ⎕TKILL dltid  ⍝ Other error - kill timeout thread
      :EndIf
      r←r
      ⍝ Clean up: deallocate thread pool and stop Jarvis server
      trg ⎕TALLOC ¯1
      _←j.Stop
    ∇

    ∇ r←AuthorizeCallback req;qParams;ns
      ⍝ Internal callback handler for OAuth authorization responses
      ⍝ Called by Jarvis when authorization server redirects to callback URL
      ⍝ Validates state, extracts authorization code, sends result to waiting thread
      :Access public
      :If '/auth'≡req.Endpoint
          (qParams←())⎕VSET↓req.QueryParams

          :If (⊂'null')≢qParams ⎕VGET⊂'error'(⊂'null')
              r←'Error: ',qParams.error_description
              qParams.success←0
              qParams ⎕TPUT ##.trg+0.1
              →0
          :EndIf

          (ns←⎕NS'').(code state)←qParams ⎕VGET (↑'code' 'state') (⊂'')

          :If 0=≢ns.code
                ns.success←0
                ns.error_description←'Code is not set'
                ns ⎕TPUT ##.trg+0.1
                r←'Error occured. Try again Later'
                →0
          :EndIf

          :If ~ns.state≡##.GetState
            ns.success←0
            ns.error_description←'State validation failed (CSRF protection)'
            ns ⎕TPUT ##.trg+0.1
            r←'Error: Invalid state'
            →0
          :EndIf

          ns.success←1
          ns ⎕TPUT ##.trg+0.1
          r←'Complete. You may close this page now.'
      :Else
          r←'404 not found'
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ LaunchURL url;_
      ⍝ Open URL in system default browser
      ⍝
      ⍝ Arguments:
      ⍝   url - URL string to open
      ⍝
      ⍝ Automatically detects platform (Windows, Linux, Mac) and uses
      ⍝ appropriate command to launch browser
      :Access public shared
      ⍝ Detect platform from APL version string (strip '-64' suffix)
      :Select '-64'~⍨⊃# ⎕WG'APLVersion'
      :Case 'Windows'
          _←⎕SHELL'start ''',url,''''       ⍝ Windows: use 'start' command
      :Case 'Linux'
          _←⎕SHELL'xdg-open "',url,'"'      ⍝ Linux: use xdg-open
      :Case 'Mac'
          _←⎕SHELL'open "',url,'"'          ⍝ Mac: use 'open' command
      :Else
          ⎕SIGNAL ⊂('EN' 11) ('Message' 'Unknown platform')
      :EndSelect
    ∇

    ∇ r←genCodeVerifier;chars
      ⍝ Generate PKCE code verifier (RFC 7636)
      ⍝ Creates cryptographically random string using unreserved characters
      ⍝ (A-Z, a-z, 0-9, -, ., _, ~) with length between 43 and 128 characters
      :Access private
      chars←⎕A,(⎕c⎕a),⎕d,'-._~'  ⍝ Unreserved characters per RFC 3986
      r←chars[(?(43+¯1+?86)/≢)chars]  ⍝ Random length 43-128, random selection
    ∇

    ∇ r←genState;chars
      ⍝ Generate CSRF protection state parameter
      ⍝ Uses Dyalog's ⎕UUID (I-beam 120⌶) to create cryptographically secure UUID
      :Access private
      r←120⌶4  ⍝ Generate UUID variant 4 (random)
    ∇

    ∇ r←genCodeChallenge codeVerifier
      ⍝ Generate PKCE code challenge from verifier
      ⍝ Applies SHA-256 hash then base64url encoding per RFC 7636
      :Access private
      r←base64 sha256 codeVerifier
    ∇

    ∇ digest←sha256 data;Init;Update;digest;ctx;Digest;dll
      ⍝ Compute SHA-256 hash of data using Conga SSL library
      ⍝ Derived from hmacsha256 implementation (In JWTAPL library)
      ⍝ Context (ctx) is 336-byte array for nettle hash state
      :Access public shared
      ⎕IO←0
      ⍝ Locate Conga SSL shared library in Dyalog installation directory
      ⍝ Searches recursively for files matching pattern conga*ssl*
      dll←∊1↓⊃1 ⎕NPARTS⊃(⎕NINFO⍠('Wildcard' 1)('Recurse' 1))'/*conga??ssl*.*',⍨(⊢2 ⎕NQ #'GetEnvironment',⊂)'Dyalog'
      ⍝ Load nettle SHA-256 functions from DLL via ⎕NA
      'Init'⎕NA dll,'|nettle_sha256_init >I1[336]'          ⍝ Initialize hash context
      'Update'⎕NA dll,'|nettle_sha256_update =I1[336] U8 <T1[]'  ⍝ Add data to hash
      'Digest'⎕NA dll,'|nettle_sha256_digest =I1[336] U8 >I1[32]'  ⍝ Finalize and get digest

      ⍝ Execute hash computation: initialize → update with data → get digest
      ctx←Init 336
      ctx←Update ctx(⍴data)data
      ctx digest←Digest ctx 32 32
    ∇

    base64←{⎕IO ⎕ML←0 1             ⍝ Base64 encoding and decoding as used in MIME.
    ⍝ From Dyalog DFNS
      chars←'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789-_'
      bits←{,⍉(⍺⍴2)⊤⍵}                   ⍝ encode each element of ⍵ in ⍺ bits,
                                        ⍝   and catenate them all together
      part←{((⍴⍵)⍴⍺↑1)⊂⍵}                ⍝ partition ⍵ into chunks of length ⍺

      0=2|⎕DR ⍵:2∘⊥∘(8∘↑)¨8 part{(-8|⍴⍵)↓⍵}6 bits{(⍵≠64)/⍵}chars⍳⍵
                                        ⍝ decode a string into octets

      four←{                             ⍝ use 4 characters to encode either
          8=⍴⍵:''∇ ⍵,0 0 0 0           ⍝   1,
          16=⍴⍵:''∇ ⍵,0 0               ⍝   2
          chars[2∘⊥¨6 part ⍵],⍺          ⍝   or 3 octets of input
      }
      cats←⊃∘(,/)∘((⊂'')∘,)              ⍝ catenate zero or more strings
      cats''∘four¨24 part 8 bits ⍵
    }
:EndClass
